# Vue Components and Structure

## Vue/Quasar Framework
This project uses:
- Vue.js 2.x
- Quasar Framework 1.x for UI components and app features
- Vuex for state management
- Vue Router for routing

## Component Structure
Components follow standard Vue.js single-file component structure:
```vue
<template>
  <!-- HTML template -->
</template>

<script>
export default {
  // Component options
}
</script>

<style>
/* Component styles */
</style>
```

## State Management
- Vuex modules are located in [src/store](mdc:src/store)
- ComponentState modules use vuex-map-fields for mapping fields

## Routing
- Routes are defined in [src/router](mdc:src/router)
- Page components are located in [src/pages](mdc:src/pages)

## Styles
- Project uses both global SCSS files in [src/css](mdc:src/css)
- Component-scoped styles
- Quasar CSS variables and classes
